  "editorReview": {
    "text": "The book excels in grounding its 'Portability Trilemma' argument in tangible details, from battery chemistry to the precise heft of a Steam Deck versus a Switch. This material focus gives its history of handheld consoles a compelling, engineering-driven spine. However, the promise of a biographical core centered on Gunpei Yokoi—so vividly established in the opening chapter—dissipates as the narrative progresses. His later contradictions and failures are left largely unexamined, which creates a noticeable structural imbalance. While the concluding synthesis offers a thoughtful perspective on 's",
